## Symptom

Room join/leave system messages and DM dead-lettering exist only in the in-memory backend. InMemoryRelay emits joined/left fan-out + history entries (relay.ml:1226-1310) and writes dead-letter rows for unknown/dead DM recipients (1124-1148); SqliteRelay join/leave are bare INSERT/DELETE with no system message, and sqlite send never records dead_letter at all (the table only grows via cross-relay forward failures). Tests asserting system messages or DLQ contents pass in-memory and describe behavior prod does not have; the sqlite dead_letter surface silently under-reports.

## Fix direction

Pick one contract and implement it in both backends (or delete the in-memory system-message path if it was never a product promise).

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17.